WEBVTT

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.040
<b>One Day in Unified Year 1966</b>

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.670
<b>A Suburb in the Allied Kingdom</b>

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.220
In those days, the Empire was 
an unstoppable superpower.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.100
First the Entente Alliance fell, then Dakia,

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.170
and then it even defeated the Republic.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.220
And while they let some survivors 
escape to the south,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.600
they'd managed to establish dominance 
over the entire continent.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.370
<b>WTN Special Correspondent
Andrew</b>

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.200
Those were the Empire's best days,
when its territory was at its largest.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.900
And yet...

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.370
<b>Former Imperial Military Development Chief Engineer
Adelheid von Schugel</b>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.880
The goddess of fate 
did not smile on the Empire.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.920
How cruel she can be.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:17.350
Why was the Empire forced to fight
a protracted battle against the entire world?

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.990
Where did they go wrong?

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.630
I wish I could answer your question,

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.860
but I'm just another lost sheep myself.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.730
I see.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:34.860
However,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.110
if I were to turn my thoughts 
towards the will of God...

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:48.530
Perhaps what drove the entire 
world to war against the Empire

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:52.130
was their terrible fear of it.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.380
Terrible fear?

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.660
Yes...

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.960
In the end, it was all about feelings!

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.250
Some felt terror!

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.040
Some felt hatred!

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.010
Some trusted it!

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.540
Some were obsessed with it!

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.300
The feelings in the hearts of all mankind

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.590
were what drove them to
follow the path of destruction!

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.850
Just as all who live by the sword 
must die by it as well.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.670
<b>Southern Continent, Unified Year 1926</b>

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.860
<i>This is 03. No enemies sighted.</i>

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.200
<i>This is 04. No contact!</i>

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.950
<i>There are no enemies anywhere to be found!</i>

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.210
Shit! We fell for a trap!

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.210
Major, what happened?

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.350
<i>The report that
they'd split their forces was false.</i>

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.930
<i>The enemy has concentrated themselves!</i>

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:48.460
<i>They prepared a trap of sweet honey 
for us, and we let it lure us out!</i>

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.210
<i>If they're not here with us,</i>

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.870
<i>the enemy must be concentrated 
in front of our main force.</i>

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.800
As planned,

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.640
we were able to lure the enemy out of 
their holes with false information.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.570
Now all that remains is to wipe them out.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.570
<b>Free Republic Military
Lt. Colonel Severin Bientot</b>

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.580
<b>Free Republic Military
General Pierre Michelaud du Lugo</b>

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.570
We've won!

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.200
It's no good! I can't get a hold of HQ!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.990
<i>Your orders, Major?</i>

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.950
Everyone, form up! We turn around 
and go as fast as we can!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.870
<i>We have the option of 
taking out their mages.</i>

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.230
Forget the small targets!

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.920
We're going to blow the shit 
out of the bastard's HQ!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.660
We're breaking through their center?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.390
<i>Major, are you serious?</i>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.870
Think about our numerical inferiority!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.130
If we just go support the main force, 
we'll only delay the inevitable!

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.770
Which means...

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.590
We flip the chess board!

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.970
And change the rules of the game!

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:35.850
Right!

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.350
A warning?

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.080
It says an enemy mage unit 
is approaching rapidly...

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.570
What? From where?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.980
Advance!

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.370
Show them no fear!

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.640
These failures abandoned their homeland!

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.830
Slaughter them to the last man!

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.600
They're about to break through 
the 12th Mage Battalion!

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.070
D-Don't tell me...

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.670
Their goal is... <i>us</i>?

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.080
<i>I can't believe I have to 
do this every damn time.</i>

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.460
<i>Being X, you piece of shit!</i>

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.310
<i>But right now, my priority is survival.</i>

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:49.340
<i>And since I need to do what I need to do...</i>

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:04.330
Holy apostles, do not forget 
the power of your God.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.770
Gather beneath his light and 
submit to the fate he has given you.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.250
All traitors to our God must burn.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.200
Target: Enemy HQ!

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.920
Fire!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.940
Evacuate! Evacuate!

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.440
Hurry!

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.420
Damn it! So it's the Rhine all over again?

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:29.960
I'm sorry, sir!

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.530
Did you see that?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.240
<b>Imperial Army
203rd Aerial Mage Battalion</b>

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.230
Talk about a castle built on sand.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.240
<b>Battalion Commander
Major Tanya von Degurechaff</b>

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.080
<b>3rd Company Commander
First Lieutenant Wilibald Koenig</b>

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.090
That was easier than expected.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.710
<b>4th Company Commander
First Lieutenant Rhiner Neumann</b>

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.700
They're too slow!

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:04.120
I'm ashamed I was unable to 
properly escort the major.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:04.130
<b>Vice Commander and 2nd Company Commander
Captain Matheus Johann Weiss</b>

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:08.420
For all their talk of class,
those escargots were pretty crude.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.420
<b>2nd Company
First Lieutenant Warren Grantz</b>

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.920
Escargot's so yummy, though!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.930
<b>1st Company, Adjutant
First Lieutenant Viktoriya Ivanovna Serebryakov</b>

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.820
Men, I know how you feel, but knock it off.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.760
This is, in theory, a battlefield.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.140
Of course! My apologies, ma'am!

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.890
But we were ordered to return 
to the Fatherland, weren't we?

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.410
Let's let our allies handle the rest of this,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.900
and get the hell out of this sandy shithole!

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.260
Let's take some drink and presents
from the Southern Continent,

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.950
and enjoy our first vacation in ages!

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.660
We can wash the sand off our bodies,

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:49.630
and finally get a good night's rest...

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.810
H-How?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:06.150
How did this happen?!

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.840
<b>Hours Before</b>

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.960
<b>Imperial Capital Berun</b>

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.470
<b>Imperial Military Airbase</b>

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:43.320
We're home!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.940
We were so far from home!

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.680
Okay, let's drink until we drop dead!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.520
Let's go to Zolka Cafeteria.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.020
Great idea! Or maybe head outside town?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.080
You're home?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:59.570
Tanya von Degurechaff, with the 
203rd Aerial Mage Battalion,

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:03.340
reporting directly to Imperial 
Strategic Headquarters, has returned.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:10.960
<b>Imperial Military Strategic Headquarters Strategy and Operations Bureau
Lt. Colonel Erich von Rerugen</b>

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:04.570
Well done.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.230
You accomplished great things down south.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.960
I was extremely impressed 
when I read the reports.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.220
You honor me too highly.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.140
I'm sure there were many unique 
difficulties you faced in the desert.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.340
By the way,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.510
how is your unit?

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.560
Casualties were minimal.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.350
We returned home with no serious losses.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.950
How is morale? You've been involved
in a long series of battles.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:31.870
Morale is high. The men are in great spirits.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.860
You really are our ace battalion.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:38.610
Let's talk about your next mission, then.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.160
About your transport...

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.740
Oh, you know Major Uger, 
with our railroads division.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:47.390
And this is Captain Rudolph, 
with Strategic Recon.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.630
R-Recon?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:04.850
<b>Early Morning, March 15th, Unified Year 1926</b>

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.860
<b>Airspace Above the Empire's Eastern Border</b>

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.860
<i>How could I have been so stupid?</i>

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:14.020
<i>I should've just said the unit had
suffered heavy losses, even if it was a lie!</i>

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.530
Attention!

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.600
Men, early this morning,

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.340
the Eastern Theater Forces'
437th Tactical Special Recon Platoon

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:29.110
sent out an emergency report.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:33.680
Federation units were seen
actively moving along Warning Line 1.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:39.690
Thus, due to an accidental error 
during training exercises,

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:43.670
our forces will be crossing into Federation 
territory to conduct reconnaissance.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:48.420
We will observe their forces' activities, 
and if necessary, issue a warning.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.680
We are not, however, to open hostilities.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.860
If we are forced to fight, 
we are to withdraw immediately.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.300
Of course, until war is declared, 
this is a violation of the neutrality treaty.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.570
You are to be extremely careful.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.460
That's all from me.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.680
Major, may I ask a question?

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.200
Of course, Lieutenant Serebryakov.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.330
If combat proves to be inevitable,

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.710
are we permitted to use force
to defend ourselves?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.730
They're Commies. Blow the shit out of them...

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.360
Or so I'd like to say,

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.090
but we need the Federation 
to fire the first shot.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:26.100
Until that happens, you are not permitted 
to fire under any circumstances.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.600
That... puts us in a pretty bad position.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.270
I agree with Lieutenant Grantz...

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:37.620
The plane is taking us to
the mission area at top speed.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.870
Nobody here's dumb enough to pass up an 
adventure in the kingdom of secrets, right?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.740
My battalion's gone through hell itself, 
so I believe you're all better than that.

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:51.000
Okay, let's do this, 
just like we do every time!

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.490
First the desert, then the snow, huh?

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:55.300
Fine with me!

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.850
I expect you to handle this mission
like you do every other!

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.350
Do your utmost for the Fatherland 
and the Imperial family!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.630
Glory to the Empire!

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:11.140
Glory to the Empire!

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.230
Armored trains...

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.450
AA guns...

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:50.880
Heavy machine guns...

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:52.300
And tanks.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:57.850
And those stacks are... 
live ammo and vehicle fuel?

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.100
Over here, Major.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.320
Look at that.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.170
Okay! Be careful with this stuff!

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.970
Look at the size of that thing.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.270
They brought a railway gun?

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:27.400
That's practically a declaration 
of war right there.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.080
Captain Weiss!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:34.580
Remind all the troops on standby 
that we are not to open fire first.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.670
Roger.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:44.810
Sooner or later, we're not going to be 
able to avoid the worst-case scenario.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:47.080
Do everything you can to remain hidden.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.530
Check your mid-range radios again.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:53.030
But maintain radio silence
until the absolute last minute.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:55.200
Don't screw up and hit 
the keys on accident.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:59.270
As soon as we confirm them firing 
on Imperial territory, report.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.050
M-Major...

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.350
The barrel is moving.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:01.040
If they open fire...

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.130
Th-They fired.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.920
The Federation is attacking on all fronts!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.020
This is a declaration of war!

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.640
The Federation has declared war
on the Empire.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:21.400
What does HQ say?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:25.490
All units, regardless of designation, 
are to begin combat immediately.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.120
<i>Switch to the battle response plan.</i>

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.050
<i>Release magical sealing.</i>

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:31.620
<i>All troops,</i>

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.360
prepare for the assault!

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:40.840
Any mages sighted in their troops?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.350
Not at the moment.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:42.870
Very good.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.490
We can assume the Federation is already in 
combat with our eastern theater forces.

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:51.520
We will attack the enemy's infantry 
as well as their rear lines.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.530
Be watchful for enemy reinforcements.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.810
<i>All troops have formed up!</i>

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.860
Men, don't let these Communists spread 
their filthy plague another inch!

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.890
Take up your guns and fight!

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.920
Grab 'em by the family jewels!

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:04.770
Right!

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.400
Begin the mission!

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:15.770
An enemy attack?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:16.690
That's impossible!

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.080
We're not at the front lines!

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.160
Armor piercing explosive spell ready... fire!

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.260
The railway gun! Protect the railway gun!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:41.540
Hurry! Hurry!

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.110
Load it up to capacity!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:45.160
Aim for the shells before they're loaded!

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.190
Roger!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:14.300
Doesn't look like there's much for us to do.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.240
Big. Fragile. Highly flammable.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.300
It's the ideal target!

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:21.930
Yeah.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.630
<i>Honestly, I hate war.</i>

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.020
<i>I think humans killing each other</i>

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:36.320
<i>is the worst part of human history.</i>

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:40.540
<i>It's nothing but a waste of 
materials and human resources.</i>

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.520
<i>But we're fighting Commies.</i>

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.900
<i>Totalitarians who infringe upon 
the freedom of the individual.</i>

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.620
<i>There's no getting along with Commies.</i>

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.850
<i>If I want a nice, safe life in the rear,</i>

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.180
<i>I need to take up my gun.</i>

00:15:56.420 --> 00:16:00.670
The 2nd Company has completed destroying 
the enemy railway gun.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:01.690
Well done.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:07.830
Still, it's weird that
we haven't seen any mages yet.

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:11.190
Major...

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:13.920
We've been ordered to reinforce 
the eastern forces.

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.850
They've given us full discretion on how.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.200
What's the situation on the front lines?

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.070
Fighting a delaying action, I believe.

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.580
Waiting for forces from the continent.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.950
They're holding on strong,

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.330
but they don't have the forces
to hold them back, huh?

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.280
How shall we help?

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.180
If we want to return to the border,

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.420
we need to break through 
the enemy's rear lines.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.220
Let's take the easy way this time.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.880
We take the long way back, huh?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:41.670
So we head for...

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.360
We burn their capital!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.440
Call it a strategic diversion.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.400
Their capital?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:49.640
We're not in Dakia anymore!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.730
You're a funny guy, Captain.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:57.240
Everybody knows the Commies 
have shit for AA defense.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.250
I guarantee that you could land 
a Cessna in Red Square.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.740
A Cessna?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.740
Red Square?

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:03.980
Uh, forget that.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:09.710
But even an average teenager
could break through their AA defenses.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.140
Then you're serious?

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.760
Of course.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:16.430
It's a diversion. That's why
we really target their capital.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.950
Run it through HQ first.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.930
See if there are no 
political considerations.

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.380
Roger.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.020
<i>I get to survive, I get to keep myself safe,</i>

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.630
<i>and I get to fuck with the Commies.</i>

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:32.550
<i>Three birds with one stone! 
What an awesome plan!</i>

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:33.910
<i>It's great.</i>

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.140
<i>I love it.</i>

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.780
I can't wait for HQ to give permission.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.080
<b>Same Day, Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.450
So the Federation's joining the war?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:45.410
What's going on?

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.040
Send out more recon planes from command!

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.300
Send all our forces from the center
to the eastern front!

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:52.290
Is the retreat still orderly? Do we 
know what's going on at the rear?

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:53.790
Are we mobilizing our strategic reserves?

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:54.540
Are the trains on time?

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:55.330
Men,

00:17:55.850 --> 00:18:01.550
Major Tanya von Degurechaff from the 203rd
 Aerial Mage Battalion has suggested a plan,

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:03.980
which I would like to discuss.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.100
<b>Vice Director of Strategy and Operations
Brigadier General Hans von Zettour</b>

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.860
<b>Deputy of Strategy and Operations
Brigadier General
 Kurt von Rudersdorf</b>

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:10.850
What's your opinion,
Lieutenant Colonel Rerugen?

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.550
A strike on their capital.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.720
It's the perfect diversion.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.860
I think it's worth letting her try.

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:22.450
What? Are you serious?

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.770
You're kidding!

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.870
That's ridiculous!

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:30.690
In a sense, we succeed even 
by making the attempt.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:34.860
If the Federation is forced to divert forces 
to the rear to protect their capital,

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:38.130
that limits the forces they can 
bring to bear on our lines.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.750
Easier said than done.

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:41.870
Who knows if she'll even get the chance?

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.730
It's the sort of insane adventurism 
front line officers are prone to...

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:44.720
It's impossible.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.470
Not even worth discussing.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.760
Think about it.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.230
It's Degurechaff we're talking about here.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:53.030
Degurechaff?

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:55.450
The one with the Silver Wings?

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:58.240
She's a talented warfighter.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:02.530
And as a hunting dog,
she's a combat officer of the highest class.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.980
Her attack on the Dakian capital...

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:07.440
Her decapitation strike at the Rhine...

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.190
She also destroyed the enemy HQ in the south.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:13.240
This is coming from a woman with experience.

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:15.250
She must believe she will succeed,

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.700
and is only confirming
whether the politics allow it.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:22.830
You seem to trust her an awful lot.

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:24.760
I cannot agree to this, regardless.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.980
This is the enemy capital 
we're talking about!

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:28.260
It's obviously impossible!

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.490
You don't think she's just mistaken?

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.260
Enough.

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:36.030
We don't have enough time
to enjoy a lengthy debate.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.730
Indeed.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.290
We're wasting time here.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.660
I judge that it's okay to give permission.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.650
Sir?!

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.800
Are you serious?!

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:47.210
It's reckless!

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.650
If she thinks she can do it, let her try.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:54.920
I bet a bottle from my personal 
collection that she succeeds.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.550
<b>March 16th, Somewhere in the Federation</b>

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.560
<i>Dear Mother and Grandmother,</i>

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.470
<i>How are you doing?</i>

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:17.130
<i>I've joined a certain unit as part 
of an overseas volunteer force.</i>

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:21.050
<i>The military rules mean
I can't write down any details,</i>

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.560
<i>but I'm doing well.</i>

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.810
<i>I've finally figured out how to use a gun.</i>

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.220
<i>And I have friends who
I can call comrades-in-arms.</i>

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.650
<i>But honestly,</i>

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:34.630
<i>the one thing I can't handle is the food.
It's quantity over quality.</i>

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:38.730
<i>I miss the pies I used to bake with you.</i>

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.730
<i>Lately, I've even been dreaming of them.</i>

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:46.650
<i>I'm sorry for being weak!</i>

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:51.130
<i>I need to grow up to be
a great soldier like Dad, don't I?</i>

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.710
<i>To bring about God's justice</i>

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.890
<i>and destroy the Empire that 
is the enemy of the world,</i>

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.740
<i>I'll keep doing my very best!</i>

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.020
<i>P.S...</i>

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:13.410
<i>I did something that was kind of
a big deal when I joined the military,</i>

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.640
<i>but I did it to show I was 
serious about being a soldier.</i>

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:18.550
<i>Don't worry!</i>

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:22.000
Get ready, Mary. We're almost to Moscow.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.760
<b>Unified States Volunteer
Warrant Officer Mary Sue</b>

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:24.530
It's that time already?

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:25.770
Oh no!

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.770
<b>Federation Capital Moscow</b>

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.770
<b>Moscow Station</b>

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:52.040
<b>Allied Kingdom Military Intelligence Service
Colonel Sir Isaac Dustin Drake</b>

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.000
So it's finally begun, huh, William?

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.630
Welcome to "allied" soil.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:57.040
<b>Multinational Volunteer Force
Battalion Commander (Allied Kingdom)
Lt. Colonel William Douglas Drake</b>

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:57.030
It's been a long time, Uncle.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:59.140
How are you finding Moscow?

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:03.380
Enjoying spending time with 
wonderful new friends?

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:08.120
The enemy of my enemy 
is my friend, you know?

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:12.140
I'm being friendly, like the politicians 
back home want me to be.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:16.400
Well... I'm sorry to hear that.

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:18.570
So this is Moscow, huh?

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:20.160
It's freezing.

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:21.890
Think they've got good food?

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:24.970
Looks like you have some 
wonderful friends too.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:28.700
How was your multinational force's
first journey together?

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:30.060
It went fine.

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:40.410
Everybody from the 
42nd Flying Division is safe.

00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:43.360
For now, that is.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:49.110
Sheesh... the brass always 
gets the stupidest ideas.

00:22:49.670 --> 00:22:54.620
A unit that symbolizes the progress and 
universality of mankind, was that it?

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:55.180
Yeah.

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:58.950
To defeat the singular evil
that is the Empire,

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:03.180
people of different races come together
like a rainbow stretching across the world.

00:23:03.180 --> 00:23:04.730
That's the ad slogan, anyway.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:07.810
Sounds like something
a politician would like.

00:23:07.810 --> 00:23:10.600
As you can see, it's an excellent unit.

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:14.330
If you'd like, I can let you take over.

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:17.590
I'll admit I'd prefer not to
shake hands with wolves.

00:23:17.590 --> 00:23:21.600
But I'd rather do that than
lead sheep into battle against a lion.

00:23:22.950 --> 00:23:25.140
Any interest in being a sheepdog?

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:27.320
The world's a stage.

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:31.030
Everybody has to play some role.

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:37.640
But it doesn't need to be me.

00:23:40.090 --> 00:23:41.890
You're right.

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:46.140
Let me give you one last warning.

00:23:46.410 --> 00:23:50.010
The Federation purged
every one of its own mages.

00:23:50.370 --> 00:23:52.240
They all got sent to the camps.

00:23:54.230 --> 00:23:56.250
So the rumors were true?

00:23:56.690 --> 00:24:02.250
Communists have no room for
X-factors like mages, it seems.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.010
My, my... What a wonderful "ally" we've got.

00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:17.400
Men, we're moving to a Federation facility.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:19.780
This place is no ally.

00:24:19.780 --> 00:24:23.050
Be very careful.

00:24:23.050 --> 00:24:24.200
Yes, sir!

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:28.150
<b>Somewhere in Moscow: People's Party Meeting Hall</b>

00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:31.690
That concludes the report from the front.

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:36.520
Comrade Secretary, if I may speak.

00:24:33.910 --> 00:24:36.530
<b>Internal Affairs Committee
Comrade Loria</b>

00:24:36.660 --> 00:24:39.040
<b>Party Leader
Comrade Secretary Josef</b>

00:24:37.630 --> 00:24:39.030
Go ahead.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:44.550
Thank you so much for that 
report from the front lines.

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:50.430
I cannot thank those comrades who have 
brought us this wonderful news enough.

00:24:50.430 --> 00:24:52.180
But...

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:58.320
It's unacceptable that the Empire
was ready for us to begin our attack.

00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:00.920
Why do you think that is, comrade?

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:03.390
I-I haven't the slightest...

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:06.910
Oh, you can't even come up
with an idea or two?

00:25:06.910 --> 00:25:09.060
After all, Comrade Nicolai,

00:25:09.060 --> 00:25:12.400
weren't you on quite good terms
with the Imperial Ambassador?

00:25:12.750 --> 00:25:16.910
I... I only interacted with
the Imperialists in an official capacity.

00:25:17.610 --> 00:25:22.800
You had dinner with him but a week ago,
and you now downplay the relationship?

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:26.920
Was that 20-year old wine he served good?

00:25:27.800 --> 00:25:28.590
No!

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:30.400
Comrade Secretary,

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:35.540
why don't we ask our comrade 
here for more details?

00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:37.810
Go ahead.

00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:43.650
W-Wait!

00:25:43.650 --> 00:25:44.920
Listen to me!

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:46.390
I can explain everything!

00:25:46.390 --> 00:25:48.310
I've never worked with the Empire!

00:25:48.310 --> 00:25:50.170
Hey, let me go!

00:25:52.590 --> 00:25:57.330
Comrades, I expect each of you to continue 
to give your utmost for the Motherland.

00:26:06.390 --> 00:26:09.380
Y-You really just want me
to drive around town?

00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:12.670
Yes. Just another inspection of the city.

00:26:12.970 --> 00:26:17.230
Even someone like me
needs a break every now and then.

00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:25.610
How about that one?

00:26:32.120 --> 00:26:33.600
Not great...

00:26:34.430 --> 00:26:36.270
So close.

00:26:36.270 --> 00:26:39.690
If I'd found her just a little sooner, 
she would've been ripe for the picking.

00:26:41.330 --> 00:26:42.880
What group are those idiots with?

00:26:42.880 --> 00:26:44.360
This is a no-fly zone!

00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:47.080
Is it that group of multinational volunteers?

00:26:47.080 --> 00:26:49.970
That's why you can't trust mages.

00:26:50.320 --> 00:26:55.430
I was right to send every last 
one of them to the camps.

00:27:10.550 --> 00:27:11.890
This is 02!

00:27:11.890 --> 00:27:14.150
I've succeeded in destroying Moscow Plaza!

00:27:14.150 --> 00:27:16.520
I've destroyed that ugly bronze statue!

00:27:31.790 --> 00:27:34.120
03 has destroyed the snakes' nest.

00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:37.450
I can see the secret police
fleeing in terror!

00:27:45.860 --> 00:27:50.470
So even the AP rounds we use to 
destroy enemy bases won't work?

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:54.590
This is 04. Our target isn't taking damage.

00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:56.470
It's incredibly tough!

00:27:56.470 --> 00:28:02.260
The goal of this operation is to
blow some stuff up and mock some people.

00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:05.140
Don't push it. Turn around and go.

00:28:05.140 --> 00:28:07.130
<i>Roger. Executing order immediately.</i>

00:28:07.390 --> 00:28:10.840
<i>All members of the battalion, I win the bet.</i>

00:28:11.190 --> 00:28:14.970
<i>I told you even a teenager 
could break through their AA.</i>

00:28:14.970 --> 00:28:18.000
And you were right, Major.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:21.480
I'm glad you're willing to 
accept your defeat like a man.

00:28:21.480 --> 00:28:23.100
But I will show no mercy.

00:28:23.540 --> 00:28:28.380
<i>Everyone, when you get back, feel free 
to enjoy a bottle of 02's best wine!</i>

00:28:28.380 --> 00:28:31.280
We haven't had a mission of 
that scale since the beach.

00:28:31.280 --> 00:28:34.140
I won't retreat a single step
in the face of alcohol.

00:28:34.780 --> 00:28:36.640
You've got guts, you bastards!

00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:39.350
<i>Yes! Hooray!</i>

00:28:41.340 --> 00:28:45.520
Men, I'm glad you have 
something to look forward to,

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:48.280
but work comes before recreation.

00:28:48.280 --> 00:28:50.640
Continue the attack!

00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:51.820
Roger!

00:28:53.610 --> 00:28:54.860
Now, then...

00:28:59.260 --> 00:29:03.320
So in this world, that thing was completed?

00:29:04.020 --> 00:29:08.880
Members of 1st Company,
we're taking down the big guy there.

00:29:09.200 --> 00:29:12.510
As soon as we're done, we'll attack 
the other government facilities.

00:29:12.890 --> 00:29:14.310
Activate magics.

00:29:14.310 --> 00:29:16.520
Target: that big pile of shit!

00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:19.020
Target: that big pile of shit!

00:29:19.360 --> 00:29:20.510
Fire!

00:29:24.990 --> 00:29:27.760
You might've shot an ally, 
Warrant Officer Sue.

00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:30.770
I-I'm sorry...

00:29:30.770 --> 00:29:33.030
You really are a terrible shot...

00:29:33.030 --> 00:29:35.550
Even though you're an 
incredibly talented mage.

00:29:36.090 --> 00:29:37.420
You've got that right.

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:40.840
It's the same for the rest of you.

00:29:40.840 --> 00:29:42.500
You need to get used to the gun!

00:29:42.500 --> 00:29:43.990
Make it a part of you!

00:29:43.990 --> 00:29:44.760
Yes, sir!

00:29:44.760 --> 00:29:47.300
Okay, keep firing!

00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:51.420
Our equipment's in terrible shape.

00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:54.350
And we haven't been given
enough ammunition to train with.

00:29:54.350 --> 00:29:56.790
I'd like to issue a formal complaint.

00:29:56.790 --> 00:29:58.020
I'll tell the party.

00:29:58.300 --> 00:30:01.450
Yeah, you do that.

00:30:06.040 --> 00:30:08.860
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:19.410
Wh-What's going on?

00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:40.950
Looks like their "People's Palace" 
was more fragile than it looked.

00:30:40.950 --> 00:30:43.460
Guess they shouldn't have rushed 
the construction so much.

00:30:43.460 --> 00:30:46.820
Looks like they shouldn't have 
rationed the concrete so much.

00:30:58.660 --> 00:31:00.680
You stupid Commie bastards.

00:31:00.680 --> 00:31:03.200
You've got your altitude settings
stuck on "bomber."

00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:04.970
Their aim is terrible, too.

00:31:04.970 --> 00:31:06.960
Shall we take out the emplacements?

00:31:06.960 --> 00:31:09.980
Shit or not, an enemy camp is an enemy camp.

00:31:09.980 --> 00:31:13.030
I can't think of a reason 
to take unnecessary damage.

00:31:13.030 --> 00:31:15.010
I'm sorry!

00:31:15.010 --> 00:31:16.820
Hey, Lieutenant,

00:31:16.820 --> 00:31:20.900
you had a special reason to
hate the Commies too, didn't you?

00:31:22.240 --> 00:31:25.010
I know a little about your background.

00:31:25.010 --> 00:31:26.890
It was when I was a child.

00:31:26.890 --> 00:31:28.200
I know!

00:31:28.200 --> 00:31:31.400
Let's do something a little special for you.

00:31:31.400 --> 00:31:35.320
If you're familiar with the place,
I'd like you to show me around.

00:31:37.530 --> 00:31:38.600
Are you okay?

00:31:38.600 --> 00:31:39.430
An attack?

00:31:39.430 --> 00:31:40.860
What was that attack?

00:31:40.860 --> 00:31:42.670
Vivi! Vivi!

00:31:42.670 --> 00:31:44.550
Are you okay? Vivi!

00:31:44.550 --> 00:31:48.540
Y-Yeah. I just got hit with some rubble.

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:49.860
But you're bleeding!

00:31:49.860 --> 00:31:51.010
We need a medic!

00:31:51.590 --> 00:31:55.640
M-Mary, calm down, please.

00:31:55.640 --> 00:31:59.350
Sir, the whole city's under attack!

00:31:59.350 --> 00:32:00.630
Is it the Empire?

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:02.140
The Empire...

00:32:02.140 --> 00:32:05.340
We never should've borrowed 
a Federation facility.

00:32:05.340 --> 00:32:07.060
How much damage did we take?

00:32:07.060 --> 00:32:08.630
Some injuries.

00:32:08.630 --> 00:32:11.490
That, and we lost our place to sleep here.

00:32:12.170 --> 00:32:13.540
Get the troops together.

00:32:13.540 --> 00:32:16.450
We'll stay on standby and 
move at the right time.

00:32:24.770 --> 00:32:25.620
Mary!

00:32:30.250 --> 00:32:32.810
Warrant Officer Sue, what are you doing?

00:32:32.810 --> 00:32:34.980
I can't let them get away with this.

00:32:34.980 --> 00:32:35.890
I'm going out there!

00:32:35.890 --> 00:32:37.210
You are not!

00:32:37.210 --> 00:32:38.290
Return to your position!

00:32:38.290 --> 00:32:40.680
But they hurt one of us!

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:41.850
I see. So what?

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:43.300
"So what"?

00:32:43.790 --> 00:32:47.720
The Empire may be killing the people 
of the Federation right now!

00:32:47.980 --> 00:32:49.640
Like I said, so what?

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:52.580
Even if they have a different 
ideology than us,

00:32:52.580 --> 00:32:55.570
if our allies are fighting, 
we need to be with them!

00:32:55.570 --> 00:32:57.900
That's what it means to 
be a soldier, isn't it?

00:32:58.160 --> 00:33:01.480
If you want to talk about being a soldier,
then first, follow orders!

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:09.380
<i>Attention, citizens of the Federation!</i>

00:33:09.380 --> 00:33:11.070
What is this broadcast?

00:33:11.070 --> 00:33:12.310
It's the Empire, apparently!

00:33:12.310 --> 00:33:13.690
Where do we run?

00:33:13.690 --> 00:33:15.460
Anywhere downtown is dangerous!

00:33:15.460 --> 00:33:17.380
Run to the housing projects!

00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:19.570
What is this warning?

00:33:19.570 --> 00:33:21.060
Where's it coming from?

00:33:21.060 --> 00:33:25.270
I don't know! But the Empire is 
addressing it to the citizenry!

00:33:25.270 --> 00:33:26.660
That's ridiculous!

00:33:26.660 --> 00:33:29.390
Nobody's going to trust what the Empire says!

00:33:29.390 --> 00:33:31.680
Just seal off the plaza!

00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:34.210
The Empire may bomb it again!

00:33:34.210 --> 00:33:35.490
Yes, sir!

00:33:36.040 --> 00:33:37.480
Impossible!

00:33:37.480 --> 00:33:39.620
The Empire?

00:33:40.680 --> 00:33:44.100
How could this happen?

00:34:52.390 --> 00:34:54.130
Wonderful.

00:34:56.140 --> 00:34:58.170
How beautiful.

00:34:58.170 --> 00:35:00.520
My blood feels like it's boiling over!

00:35:00.520 --> 00:35:02.420
I want her!

00:35:02.650 --> 00:35:05.180
I want her, no matter what!

00:35:07.210 --> 00:35:07.910
What's this?

00:35:11.170 --> 00:35:12.910
You bastards!

00:35:12.910 --> 00:35:14.490
Wait! Warrant Officer Sue!

00:35:19.470 --> 00:35:21.260
Shit! That idiot!

00:35:45.460 --> 00:35:48.030
You ruined the mood.

00:35:48.030 --> 00:35:50.190
Major, enemy reinforcements!

00:35:50.190 --> 00:35:53.300
Two companies' worth of mages, from our rear!

00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:56.480
Did you really get permission to engage?

00:35:56.480 --> 00:35:57.220
Yes!

00:35:57.220 --> 00:35:59.830
Your kind uncle got us the okay!

00:35:59.830 --> 00:36:02.980
We get caught up in this mess
as soon as we get here?

00:36:02.980 --> 00:36:05.180
Now we've got extra work to do, damn it.

00:36:06.300 --> 00:36:08.190
How is she so fast?

00:36:08.600 --> 00:36:10.480
Is her magical power overflowing?

00:36:10.480 --> 00:36:12.950
Mary's latent magical ability is incredible.

00:36:12.950 --> 00:36:14.700
She was far better than any of her class.

00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:17.190
So she's incompetent, and a hard worker.

00:36:17.190 --> 00:36:18.410
That's a bitch.

00:36:18.890 --> 00:36:20.580
Fall back and support.

00:36:20.580 --> 00:36:22.040
Don't try to get near her!

00:36:22.040 --> 00:36:22.790
Yes, sir!

00:36:49.780 --> 00:36:51.430
Their training is on a whole other level.

00:36:53.160 --> 00:36:55.860
Major! It doesn't seem 
to be Federation forces.

00:36:55.860 --> 00:36:58.510
What? But this is Commie airspace!

00:37:00.620 --> 00:37:03.150
Their appearance and equipment 
suggest a multinational force.

00:37:03.150 --> 00:37:04.830
What?

00:37:04.830 --> 00:37:08.240
There may be more.
Look for a chance to get out of here.

00:37:15.340 --> 00:37:16.860
Phil! Keith!

00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:23.340
She's out of ammo?

00:37:26.900 --> 00:37:28.710
Give me power, God!

00:37:30.630 --> 00:37:33.780
For peace! For justice!

00:37:33.780 --> 00:37:35.530
You're bothering me.

00:37:35.530 --> 00:37:38.360
This reminds me of something 
that happened before.

00:37:48.240 --> 00:37:50.160
A young girl?

00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:52.790
But I guess that goes for both of us.

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:08.500
Th-That's...

00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:24.230
What?

00:38:44.470 --> 00:38:45.450
Major!

00:38:45.450 --> 00:38:47.060
I think it's time to go!

00:38:47.060 --> 00:38:48.300
Let's retreat!

00:38:49.460 --> 00:38:50.940
Major!

00:38:51.930 --> 00:38:53.150
Yeah...

00:38:53.780 --> 00:38:55.220
Everyone, withdraw.

00:38:55.220 --> 00:38:57.110
Head for the rendezvous point at top speed.

00:38:57.430 --> 00:38:58.560
Roger!

00:39:12.800 --> 00:39:14.620
Mary! Mary!

00:39:13.940 --> 00:39:17.270
Warrant Officer Sue,
can you hear me? Wake up!

00:39:17.270 --> 00:39:18.080
Warrant Officer Sue!

00:39:18.630 --> 00:39:20.870
She's awake, it seems, 
but she's badly injured.

00:39:20.870 --> 00:39:23.100
Pick her up. We're heading back to base.

00:39:23.100 --> 00:39:24.630
Hang in there, Mary!

00:39:24.630 --> 00:39:26.290
Don't pass out on us!

00:39:26.950 --> 00:39:29.270
<i>Being shot with a gun hurts.</i>

00:39:30.200 --> 00:39:33.430
<i>Even more when it's Dad's gun.</i>

00:39:34.450 --> 00:39:36.420
<i>My dad was so nice...</i>

00:39:37.600 --> 00:39:40.410
<i>And she killed him.</i>

00:39:41.660 --> 00:39:44.060
<i>I'll make that demon pay.</i>

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:47.760
<i>God... God!</i>

00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:52.160
<i>Please! Give me power!</i>

00:39:54.490 --> 00:39:57.120
<b>Several Days Later</b>

00:39:57.160 --> 00:40:00.320
Extra! Extra!

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:03.870
Fatherland's flag planted on enemy territory!

00:40:03.870 --> 00:40:05.790
They burned all their flags?

00:40:05.790 --> 00:40:07.680
They took out the secret police?

00:40:07.680 --> 00:40:09.370
They even made a movie!

00:40:09.370 --> 00:40:11.900
It says they "do not believe in tears."

00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:13.890
<b>Imperial Strategic Headquarters</b>

00:40:11.900 --> 00:40:13.870
They're making fun of that 
Federation saying, huh?

00:40:15.690 --> 00:40:17.280
Why?

00:40:18.390 --> 00:40:20.440
Why did this happen?

00:40:20.890 --> 00:40:24.900
I thought they were just going to 
put some pressure on the capital.

00:40:25.470 --> 00:40:29.900
I didn't think they'd destroy every 
political symbol of the Federation,

00:40:29.900 --> 00:40:34.300
put up a flag, and sing our anthem.

00:40:38.300 --> 00:40:40.160
That's going too far.

00:40:42.960 --> 00:40:47.780
At least we completely achieved
our goal of a strategic distraction.

00:40:48.200 --> 00:40:49.800
Lieutenant Colonel,

00:40:49.800 --> 00:40:54.710
it seems that even you
underestimated the major's powers.

00:40:54.710 --> 00:40:58.570
It was the perfect distraction, in fact.

00:40:58.570 --> 00:41:01.730
And the people are saying 
it's a historic achievement.

00:41:04.200 --> 00:41:07.470
The problem is the politicians.

00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:12.120
We won't be able to submit
a peace proposal for a while.

00:41:12.430 --> 00:41:16.610
Not after we completely crushed their pride.

00:41:16.900 --> 00:41:21.710
In their anger, the Federation's 
sure to send even more forces now.

00:41:21.710 --> 00:41:25.780
We need to come up with
a plan for the next stage.

00:41:28.810 --> 00:41:30.330
<i>Degurechaff...</i>

00:41:31.830 --> 00:41:35.120
<i>When she gets back,
I'm going to strangle her!</i>

00:41:35.720 --> 00:41:37.470
<b>March 26, 1926</b>

00:41:37.850 --> 00:41:39.600
<b>Imperial Eastern Front Temporary Base 21</b>

00:41:39.590 --> 00:41:41.090
Cheers!

00:41:41.580 --> 00:41:43.210
How many times have we done that?

00:41:43.210 --> 00:41:45.140
You can toast as many times as you like!

00:41:45.140 --> 00:41:46.850
Drink! Drink!

00:41:46.850 --> 00:41:50.090
That attack on the capital 
was a stroke of genius!

00:41:50.090 --> 00:41:53.010
That's why you're Strategic HQ's ace unit!

00:41:53.010 --> 00:41:55.870
You sure showed those Commies!

00:42:03.860 --> 00:42:08.470
Captain, you remember the deal, right?

00:42:08.470 --> 00:42:11.990
I'm glad you're willing to 
accept your defeat like a man.

00:42:11.990 --> 00:42:13.880
But I will show no mercy.

00:42:13.880 --> 00:42:18.180
Everyone, when you get back, feel free 
to enjoy a bottle of 02's best wine!

00:42:22.820 --> 00:42:24.980
You've got more than we thought!

00:42:24.980 --> 00:42:27.390
You sell what you brought back 
from the south to stock up?

00:42:27.390 --> 00:42:30.180
You're a fan of the good stuff, huh?

00:42:32.650 --> 00:42:35.440
Sorry, but not as much as you are!

00:42:39.020 --> 00:42:41.360
"Aaah," my ass!

00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:43.450
This was mine to begin with!

00:42:45.390 --> 00:42:46.810
He's going really hard!

00:42:46.810 --> 00:42:48.690
Is he going to be okay?

00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:51.160
I'm scared. He's gonna be 
a pain to deal with later.

00:42:53.770 --> 00:42:59.480
<i>In any era, drinking has a certain effect
in bringing people together.</i>

00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:05.160
<i>It's tough.</i>

00:43:05.890 --> 00:43:06.970
Major!

00:43:07.940 --> 00:43:09.930
How about some dessert?

00:43:10.890 --> 00:43:12.490
Fruit punch!

00:43:12.890 --> 00:43:15.020
Lieutenant!

00:43:15.020 --> 00:43:17.360
Are you giving the major 
my liquor-preserved fruits?

00:43:17.660 --> 00:43:20.070
You can't do that! You can't!

00:43:20.070 --> 00:43:23.150
There's no alcohol in them.

00:43:23.150 --> 00:43:25.580
They're specially made to be sweet.

00:43:26.780 --> 00:43:28.570
Drunks.

00:43:28.570 --> 00:43:31.630
Don't worry about me.

00:43:31.630 --> 00:43:35.700
I think I have an illness that
definitely needs 24 hours to wear off.

00:43:35.700 --> 00:43:38.080
Don't wake me up for anything but a mission.

00:43:39.930 --> 00:43:43.240
Let yourselves go, but don't get to the point

00:43:43.240 --> 00:43:45.680
where it interferes with your duties.

00:43:48.720 --> 00:43:52.110
The major, who's like a living,
breathing rulebook...

00:43:52.110 --> 00:43:55.430
The major, who's a demon 
obsessed with military code...

00:43:55.430 --> 00:43:57.180
Told us to...

00:43:57.180 --> 00:43:59.440
...let ourselves go?

00:43:59.440 --> 00:44:01.810
Attention, everyone!

00:44:02.610 --> 00:44:06.710
Our battalion commander
has retired due to illness.

00:44:06.710 --> 00:44:07.310
Seriously?

00:44:07.310 --> 00:44:08.290
Lucky us!

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:10.120
And so...

00:44:10.380 --> 00:44:15.130
Let's have another toast to 
Major Degurechaff's health!

00:44:15.130 --> 00:44:17.850
Cheers!

00:44:33.850 --> 00:44:35.520
<i>It's tough.</i>

00:44:44.820 --> 00:44:46.330
<i>That toughness...</i>

00:44:46.980 --> 00:44:50.500
<i>wasn't normal. Not at all.</i>

00:45:03.690 --> 00:45:07.650
<i>That sturdiness, the amount of magic...</i>

00:45:08.180 --> 00:45:09.800
<i>It has to be.</i>

00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:16.740
<i>That insane fanatic!</i>

00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:22.400
Your ability to recover is impressive.

00:45:22.690 --> 00:45:25.550
I planned to have you get a longer rest.

00:45:25.550 --> 00:45:27.530
I can't rest.

00:45:27.530 --> 00:45:31.750
We need to show the people of 
the Federation why we're here.

00:45:31.750 --> 00:45:34.750
You don't have the right 
to argue that with me.

00:45:35.080 --> 00:45:37.890
The volunteer force is
a high-level political matter.

00:45:39.920 --> 00:45:42.470
Our ally's capital was attacked.

00:45:42.810 --> 00:45:44.890
We're not going to help them?

00:45:44.890 --> 00:45:48.480
It's their fault for not being 
able to properly protect it.

00:45:48.480 --> 00:45:50.260
We did nothing wrong.

00:45:50.610 --> 00:45:52.650
You want us to just be observers?!

00:45:53.650 --> 00:45:58.410
We came together to destroy the Empire,
our common enemy!

00:45:58.410 --> 00:46:00.410
For humanity! For the world!

00:46:00.410 --> 00:46:02.200
We should all fight together!

00:46:05.320 --> 00:46:07.820
You want revenge that badly?

00:46:11.330 --> 00:46:13.610
I know about your past.

00:46:13.920 --> 00:46:18.240
Your father died in combat 
with the Empire, yes?

00:46:18.240 --> 00:46:21.110
I can understand your hatred for the enemy.

00:46:21.440 --> 00:46:22.710
But...

00:46:23.210 --> 00:46:26.590
We're not murderers or avengers.

00:46:27.050 --> 00:46:28.400
We're soldiers.

00:46:29.460 --> 00:46:33.090
We're not fighting this war 
out of personal feelings.

00:46:38.590 --> 00:46:40.510
We're leaving Moscow in the morning.

00:46:40.510 --> 00:46:44.900
If you're a soldier, don't conflate our enemy
and the object of your vengeance.

00:47:02.010 --> 00:47:06.390
Within the Empire,
there's a demon I must defeat!

00:47:16.600 --> 00:47:18.800
Everyone, wake up!

00:47:22.150 --> 00:47:23.640
What's going on?

00:47:25.020 --> 00:47:27.690
Captain Weiss! Is Captain Weiss here?

00:47:27.690 --> 00:47:29.430
Yes, ma'am!

00:47:29.430 --> 00:47:32.710
Captain Weiss, Strategic HQ
sent us a love letter.

00:47:32.710 --> 00:47:34.540
Get the battalion together.

00:47:34.540 --> 00:47:36.040
Yes, ma'am!

00:47:36.040 --> 00:47:37.200
Hurry!

00:47:37.690 --> 00:47:40.090
We'll begin the briefing as soon you're done.

00:47:43.180 --> 00:47:46.790
It's been 10 days since the start of the war,
and the borders have moved a lot.

00:47:46.790 --> 00:47:48.660
Look at how the enemy's moving.

00:47:52.470 --> 00:47:53.880
There are three general groups.

00:47:54.690 --> 00:47:56.980
Group A, moving to the north.

00:47:56.980 --> 00:48:00.100
Group B, readying for
an attack on the Empire itself.

00:48:00.100 --> 00:48:05.140
And Group C, which has started 
to move towards Dakia.

00:48:05.140 --> 00:48:09.270
It's believed that Group B,
the one in the center, is their largest.

00:48:09.270 --> 00:48:11.400
But there's no reason 
to just face it head on.

00:48:11.800 --> 00:48:15.030
Strategic HQ wants to start at 
the north and strike them first,

00:48:15.030 --> 00:48:18.040
then head down to strike and encircle 
the main force from their flank.

00:48:19.670 --> 00:48:22.660
Then what's our job?

00:48:23.680 --> 00:48:25.980
To act as a mobile flying column.

00:48:25.980 --> 00:48:29.700
We'll be going ahead of the main units from 
central command that are heading north.

00:48:29.700 --> 00:48:33.440
But we can't ignore the pressure 
Group B is putting on us.

00:48:33.800 --> 00:48:36.180
Their sheer numbers make them
difficult to deal with.

00:48:36.570 --> 00:48:41.170
Can the center hold while 
we're destroying Group A?

00:48:41.170 --> 00:48:42.920
Captain Weiss...

00:48:43.490 --> 00:48:45.360
Remember this.

00:48:45.360 --> 00:48:48.030
It's not the numbers on paper. 
It's what's inside that counts.

00:48:50.030 --> 00:48:53.670
Communists believe that 
the party is always right.

00:48:53.670 --> 00:48:57.030
They put politics above military logic.

00:48:57.320 --> 00:48:59.800
And if you go against that, you're purged.

00:48:59.800 --> 00:49:03.660
Do you want to tell me an army 
like that is a <i>real</i> army?

00:49:06.350 --> 00:49:07.410
Come in.

00:49:07.410 --> 00:49:08.980
Excuse me.

00:49:08.980 --> 00:49:10.930
Emergency request from the eastern forces.

00:49:11.270 --> 00:49:12.150
What?

00:49:14.340 --> 00:49:19.250
The 3rd and 32nd Divisions that are serving
as the rear guard for withdrawal

00:49:19.250 --> 00:49:21.850
are being surrounded at Tiegenhoff.

00:49:22.510 --> 00:49:23.670
What about the eastern forces?

00:49:23.670 --> 00:49:25.440
This is their job.

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:29.200
They've expended their strategic reserves
in the battles so far.

00:49:29.200 --> 00:49:33.980
So they've come begging to the unit 
under Strategic HQ's direct command?

00:49:33.980 --> 00:49:35.760
Urban combat, huh?

00:49:35.760 --> 00:49:39.190
If the enemy has it heavily encircled, 
won't it be difficult to rescue them?

00:49:39.520 --> 00:49:43.700
Aerial photography from the area 
doesn't show any heavy guns.

00:49:44.190 --> 00:49:47.460
All we've been able to confirm is 
a small number of field artillery pieces.

00:49:47.460 --> 00:49:50.810
Heavy guns are incredibly slow.

00:49:50.810 --> 00:49:54.480
The Federation's got the same problems 
moving the things as we do.

00:49:54.480 --> 00:50:00.480
But it's possible that there are long-range
railway guns deployed near the border.

00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:01.870
That's true.

00:50:01.870 --> 00:50:05.360
Something their size could 
cause serious damage.

00:50:07.090 --> 00:50:11.000
You're right to not 
underestimate your enemy.

00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:14.830
But even railway guns 
aren't a serious threat.

00:50:15.890 --> 00:50:21.610
In all our battles against the Federation,
we've yet to see a single observer mage.

00:50:21.610 --> 00:50:25.630
Even if their infantry 
have observers with them,

00:50:25.630 --> 00:50:28.370
its not realistic for them
to adapt on the fly.

00:50:28.370 --> 00:50:30.550
You're right, come to think of it.

00:50:30.550 --> 00:50:32.600
So it's possible to save them.

00:50:32.990 --> 00:50:39.010
But the 203rd Battalion has already 
received orders from Strategic HQ.

00:50:39.630 --> 00:50:43.390
We report directly to Strategic HQ.

00:50:44.270 --> 00:50:46.570
<i>So both of them need our help, huh?</i>

00:50:47.260 --> 00:50:52.410
But a partial victory that leads 
to an overall defeat is worthless.

00:50:52.410 --> 00:50:54.850
I hate to do this to the eastern forces,

00:50:54.850 --> 00:50:58.390
but for the sake of our whole army, 
we should do the flying column mission.

00:50:58.390 --> 00:51:00.830
I hate to say it, but you're right.

00:51:01.170 --> 00:51:03.310
We'll just have to pray for Tiegenhoff.

00:51:09.880 --> 00:51:11.110
Major?

00:51:11.110 --> 00:51:12.770
What's wrong?

00:51:12.770 --> 00:51:15.270
This is an interesting position.

00:51:15.270 --> 00:51:16.850
Lieutenant Serebryakov...

00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:18.850
Bring me a more detailed map.

00:51:18.850 --> 00:51:19.790
Yes, ma'am.

00:51:19.790 --> 00:51:21.250
A railway map, too.

00:51:29.030 --> 00:51:32.030
Tiegenhoff is in a good position.

00:51:32.030 --> 00:51:36.110
You could say it's a critical point in 
Strategic HQ's northern operations.

00:51:37.530 --> 00:51:38.990
I see!

00:51:39.290 --> 00:51:42.400
Aerial photography shows
the rail lines are undamaged!

00:51:42.400 --> 00:51:47.170
We'll be able to resupply for our flying 
column mission at regular intervals.

00:51:47.530 --> 00:51:49.700
It's on a river and easy to defend,

00:51:49.700 --> 00:51:52.600
and also a fair distance away 
from the eastern borders.

00:51:52.600 --> 00:51:56.620
And we should be able to apply pressure to 
strategic transit points from there as well.

00:51:56.620 --> 00:51:58.630
It's the perfect base!

00:51:59.810 --> 00:52:01.890
Wonderful.

00:52:02.600 --> 00:52:05.870
Rescuing Tiegenhoff is 
the ultimate aufheben.

00:52:05.870 --> 00:52:10.520
We can give both the eastern forces 
and Strategic HQ what they want.

00:52:10.890 --> 00:52:12.140
We're gonna do it.

00:52:12.570 --> 00:52:13.300
Right!

00:52:15.690 --> 00:52:17.330
So we're saving people, huh?

00:52:18.020 --> 00:52:19.900
Lieutenant Serebryakov,

00:52:19.900 --> 00:52:22.790
have the troops load up 
all the medical supplies they can carry.

00:52:22.790 --> 00:52:23.570
Roger that!

00:52:23.570 --> 00:52:26.450
It would be nice if we could take 
some whiskey and cigarettes,

00:52:26.450 --> 00:52:29.230
but we barely have any to begin with.

00:52:29.230 --> 00:52:32.110
Don't worry about that, Major.

00:52:32.830 --> 00:52:34.090
Actually...

00:52:34.470 --> 00:52:37.780
We won a bunch from the eastern 
forces playing cards yesterday.

00:52:37.780 --> 00:52:40.890
I was going to put them in 
the battalion's warehouse,

00:52:40.890 --> 00:52:43.130
but we should share them with our allies!

00:52:43.130 --> 00:52:45.310
I can't believe you, Captain Weiss.

00:52:45.580 --> 00:52:50.470
I thought you had more discipline
as an officer.

00:52:50.470 --> 00:52:54.710
No, it was Lieutenant Serebryakov,
not me, who took their stuff.

00:53:05.530 --> 00:53:06.870
We're counting on you!

00:53:06.870 --> 00:53:08.530
Save our allies!

00:53:08.530 --> 00:53:10.730
Rescue Tiegenhoff!

00:53:16.540 --> 00:53:21.050
<b>Imperial City of Tiegenhoff</b>

00:53:38.440 --> 00:53:42.820
<b>Imperial 49th Mage Battalion: Major Jotuck Hofen</b>

00:53:38.720 --> 00:53:41.660
There are so many! Give it up, damn it!

00:53:41.660 --> 00:53:42.820
Major!

00:53:42.820 --> 00:53:44.220
There's not enough of us!

00:53:44.220 --> 00:53:47.260
Our defenses to the northeast 
won't last much longer!

00:53:48.560 --> 00:53:51.400
Shit! I need help, and I don't care
where it comes from.

00:53:51.400 --> 00:53:54.430
I'm not even gonna ask questions!

00:53:54.430 --> 00:53:56.960
<i>Tiegenhoff Control to 49th Mage Battalion.</i>

00:53:57.330 --> 00:53:59.450
<i>Reinforcements are on their way.</i>

00:53:59.450 --> 00:54:00.730
<i>Watch for them.</i>

00:54:08.690 --> 00:54:09.890
Allies?

00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:11.780
You came!

00:54:18.520 --> 00:54:21.770
Anti-ground bombardment! Aim at will!

00:54:21.770 --> 00:54:23.290
Fire!

00:54:36.800 --> 00:54:38.560
I am Major Hofen,

00:54:38.560 --> 00:54:42.150
with the 49th Mage Battalion 
of the 3rd Division.

00:54:42.150 --> 00:54:43.890
Major Degurechaff,

00:54:43.890 --> 00:54:48.040
of the 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 
reporting directly to Strategic HQ.

00:54:48.040 --> 00:54:50.880
I'm terribly sorry
we couldn't get here sooner.

00:54:52.090 --> 00:54:53.320
Is there a problem?

00:54:53.600 --> 00:54:54.940
N-No...

00:54:54.940 --> 00:54:57.130
Thank you for coming!

00:54:57.130 --> 00:55:00.820
We only survived because you got 
here before their heavy guns did.

00:55:00.820 --> 00:55:03.520
I'm glad we made it.

00:55:03.800 --> 00:55:06.800
HQ is this way. I'll take you there.

00:55:11.280 --> 00:55:15.620
Our job will be to protect HQ 
and wipe out their survivors.

00:55:15.620 --> 00:55:16.700
What about you?

00:55:16.700 --> 00:55:19.630
We'll use this city as our base

00:55:19.630 --> 00:55:22.890
and carry out the flying column order
that we were given by Strategic HQ.

00:55:22.890 --> 00:55:25.220
They're pretty rough on us.

00:55:25.220 --> 00:55:26.550
I see.

00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:30.560
I can understand why, given how 
highly-trained you looked.

00:55:30.820 --> 00:55:32.450
I'm honored.

00:55:32.900 --> 00:55:36.970
I'd love to have a drink with you...

00:55:37.300 --> 00:55:40.230
But I'll buy one for your men, someday.

00:55:40.230 --> 00:55:44.680
I'm afraid my men are heavy drinkers.

00:55:44.680 --> 00:55:48.740
They might bankrupt you, I think.

00:55:50.660 --> 00:55:51.770
All right, then!

00:55:51.770 --> 00:55:54.650
My whole battalion will pay for them!

00:55:54.650 --> 00:55:57.160
Drink all you like!

00:55:57.160 --> 00:55:59.910
My men will be happy to hear that!

00:56:02.610 --> 00:56:05.350
I'll be going, then.

00:56:08.310 --> 00:56:09.400
Major!

00:56:09.890 --> 00:56:13.410
Was that the officer who came to save us?

00:56:13.410 --> 00:56:14.400
Yes.

00:56:14.710 --> 00:56:19.880
The rumors that Strategic HQ had
a child officer were true, it seems.

00:56:20.300 --> 00:56:24.520
That legend of the battlefield 
was surprisingly true.

00:56:28.450 --> 00:56:31.600
Comrades, the situation is dire!

00:56:29.780 --> 00:56:37.040
<b>Federation Front Lines</b>

00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:34.580
Our main force is barely managing 
to continue their advance,

00:56:34.580 --> 00:56:37.040
but the lack of heavy guns
is a huge problem.

00:56:37.290 --> 00:56:39.160
<b>Federation Rear Echelon</b>

00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:39.170
That's right.

00:56:39.170 --> 00:56:42.910
The front lines say the situation 
is "difficult, but manageable."

00:56:39.410 --> 00:56:42.920
<b>Federation Army
Political Officer</b>

00:56:43.240 --> 00:56:46.300
Some heavy guns would be appreciated 
if they're available.

00:56:46.300 --> 00:56:49.760
<b>Federation Capital Moscow</b>

00:56:46.610 --> 00:56:49.750
Comrades, I'm told everything 
is going "almost perfectly"!

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:54.020
Our forces are advancing with 
an overwhelming advantage.

00:56:54.330 --> 00:56:57.030
There's no need to wait for 
the arrival of heavy guns.

00:56:57.030 --> 00:57:00.180
The mission is almost complete.

00:57:00.610 --> 00:57:03.270
Thank you for the good news.

00:57:03.570 --> 00:57:07.730
Comrade Secretary, I have 
some other good news.

00:57:07.730 --> 00:57:09.500
Speak.

00:57:09.770 --> 00:57:10.590
Yes.

00:57:11.100 --> 00:57:16.980
That enemy unit is in Tiegenhoff right now.

00:57:17.240 --> 00:57:18.990
"That enemy unit"?

00:57:18.990 --> 00:57:23.750
The ones who did <i>that</i>, 
if you follow my meaning.

00:57:25.490 --> 00:57:28.520
An unforgivably barbaric offense!

00:57:28.520 --> 00:57:32.050
Just thinking about it makes my blood boil!

00:57:32.670 --> 00:57:36.930
There's no reason to let them live.

00:57:36.930 --> 00:57:41.360
The overwhelming numbers
given to us by the Motherland!

00:57:41.860 --> 00:57:46.420
And the air planes birthed 
by our technology!

00:57:46.420 --> 00:57:47.850
And then...

00:57:48.290 --> 00:57:52.110
While they are a filthy 
imperialist curse...

00:57:52.110 --> 00:57:57.240
We can also send in
the multinational volunteers!

00:57:57.240 --> 00:58:00.990
We'll send everything we've got at them!

00:58:00.990 --> 00:58:02.500
Torment them!

00:58:02.500 --> 00:58:03.500
Torture them!

00:58:03.500 --> 00:58:06.120
And obliterate them!

00:58:15.220 --> 00:58:17.630
My beloved Comrade Secretary...

00:58:18.110 --> 00:58:22.250
I propose a large-scale assault
on Tiegenhoff.

00:58:23.520 --> 00:58:25.770
<b>March 28, Unified Year 1926</b>

00:58:26.020 --> 00:58:28.520
<b>Federation Airfield</b>

00:58:28.760 --> 00:58:30.810
Are we not done resupplying yet?

00:58:30.810 --> 00:58:32.600
We don't have enough people!

00:58:32.600 --> 00:58:34.530
We can't go any faster!

00:58:35.400 --> 00:58:36.940
Real combat, huh?

00:58:36.940 --> 00:58:39.640
I never thought we'd fight on
the same side as the Federation.

00:58:39.640 --> 00:58:41.270
We can do this.

00:58:41.600 --> 00:58:43.090
Damn...

00:58:43.540 --> 00:58:45.810
How did this happen?

00:58:45.810 --> 00:58:47.280
Lieutenant Colonel Drake...

00:58:48.300 --> 00:58:50.220
We're fighting the Empire, right?

00:58:50.220 --> 00:58:52.480
We get to fight too, right?

00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:55.650
Only in accordance with orders from home,
and as much as they allow us.

00:58:56.120 --> 00:58:58.440
That's part of God's will too, I'm sure.

00:58:58.440 --> 00:58:59.940
Right.

00:58:59.940 --> 00:59:03.180
I hope you don't end up meeting that 
God of yours sooner than you want to.

00:59:03.610 --> 00:59:05.440
"Do not test the Lord."

00:59:05.440 --> 00:59:08.190
I will simply do my duty.

00:59:12.620 --> 00:59:14.650
That's a wonderful look 
you have on your face.

00:59:14.650 --> 00:59:17.040
Do you miss the sea so badly?

00:59:17.040 --> 00:59:21.540
Yes. I'd love to be kicking 
back in a pub right now.

00:59:21.540 --> 00:59:23.490
You think it's a stupid order?

00:59:23.920 --> 00:59:25.490
That's right.

00:59:25.490 --> 00:59:29.830
The politicians back home must really want 
to get in the Federation's good graces.

00:59:29.830 --> 00:59:33.510
And they're sacrificing a unit filled 
with nothing but rookies to do it.

00:59:33.510 --> 00:59:35.090
Are they insane?

00:59:35.540 --> 00:59:38.130
Who knows how much we'll have to 
pay the widows in pensions?

00:59:38.900 --> 00:59:41.710
By the way, is that her?

00:59:42.850 --> 00:59:46.040
Yes. Warrant Officer Mary Sue.

00:59:47.110 --> 00:59:50.010
Her father was a brave soldier.

00:59:50.530 --> 00:59:52.620
I know you've no obligation to do this,

00:59:53.100 --> 00:59:56.170
but please keep an eye on her
as much as you can.

01:00:06.690 --> 01:00:09.120
Major! Major!

01:00:09.120 --> 01:00:11.510
Wake up! Major!

01:00:11.510 --> 01:00:13.120
What is it?

01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:15.790
An attack! The Federation is attacking!

01:00:16.710 --> 01:00:18.050
How many?

01:00:18.470 --> 01:00:20.760
Eight divisions at a minimum.

01:00:20.760 --> 01:00:22.220
Eight divisions?

01:00:22.220 --> 01:00:24.230
That's the initial report 
from our air fleet.

01:00:24.230 --> 01:00:25.720
That's four times what we have!

01:00:25.720 --> 01:00:29.220
Yes. And that's the most 
optimistic estimate.

01:00:32.240 --> 01:00:36.750
They shouldn't have realized how 
important Tiegenhoff is yet!

01:00:36.750 --> 01:00:41.240
But they're abandoning their plans
for a bold offensive?

01:00:41.240 --> 01:00:44.000
<i>Commies aren't allowed to be that adaptable!</i>

01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:45.990
<i>Did they figure out my plan?</i>

01:00:45.990 --> 01:00:47.770
<i>Or did something leak?</i>

01:00:48.070 --> 01:00:49.000
<i>Shit!</i>

01:00:49.000 --> 01:00:50.250
<i>How?</i>

01:00:54.640 --> 01:00:57.590
W-Well, the enemy is human, too.

01:00:57.590 --> 01:00:59.800
They can't get their heavy 
equipment here in time.

01:00:59.800 --> 01:01:03.090
They'll use their light forces 
to execute an attack first.

01:01:03.090 --> 01:01:06.590
At this rate, we might lose our new base.

01:01:06.590 --> 01:01:08.920
Wake everyone up, now!

01:01:30.210 --> 01:01:33.920
Comrades, what has our homeland done?

01:01:34.330 --> 01:01:36.090
The answer is simple.

01:01:36.090 --> 01:01:38.240
We did nothing.

01:01:38.680 --> 01:01:39.890
Nothing.

01:01:40.300 --> 01:01:44.530
But the Federation is attacking us.
They want to kill us.

01:01:44.530 --> 01:01:47.270
It's impossible for us to be good neighbors.

01:01:47.270 --> 01:01:50.650
This world isn't fair at all, it seems.

01:01:51.190 --> 01:01:54.650
If they wish to violate our rights,

01:01:54.960 --> 01:01:56.640
we must fight!

01:01:58.240 --> 01:02:01.100
I love freedom above all else.

01:02:01.120 --> 01:02:02.740
I will secure freedom,

01:02:02.740 --> 01:02:04.240
I will protect freedom,

01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:05.730
and I will defend freedom to the last!

01:02:06.290 --> 01:02:08.440
We cannot retreat from this battle!

01:02:08.990 --> 01:02:12.470
Comrades, this is a battle for freedom!

01:02:12.470 --> 01:02:14.530
The slightest hesitation 
will not be allowed!

01:02:15.210 --> 01:02:17.890
We're kicking these Commies 
out of our country!

01:02:18.150 --> 01:02:19.870
We will have victory!

01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:21.870
Or we will have death!

01:02:21.870 --> 01:02:24.640
We are the guards of our country's gates!

01:02:36.900 --> 01:02:38.900
<b>Battle of Tiegenhoff</b>

01:02:39.150 --> 01:02:41.440
<b>3 Hours Since the Start of the Battle</b>

01:02:43.160 --> 01:02:45.740
Wh-What the hell is this?

01:02:46.620 --> 01:02:48.900
I can't believe how many there are!

01:03:18.230 --> 01:03:20.510
Don't let them scare you! Fire! Fire!

01:03:49.130 --> 01:03:52.370
Shit! Can't we do something 
about those tanks?

01:04:00.770 --> 01:04:03.280
Mages? We're saved!

01:04:03.590 --> 01:04:05.650
Now! Fire! Fire!

01:04:05.990 --> 01:04:07.290
Don't let up!

01:04:07.290 --> 01:04:09.770
The enemy's offensive has been blunted!

01:04:09.770 --> 01:04:12.540
We outnumber them!

01:04:12.540 --> 01:04:15.650
Shit! They just keep coming!

01:04:14.920 --> 01:04:16.370
Where's our air support?!

01:04:16.370 --> 01:04:17.890
Stop them no matter what!

01:04:17.890 --> 01:04:20.080
Where the hell is she?

01:04:19.310 --> 01:04:21.090
Let's go! Charge!

01:04:21.090 --> 01:04:23.520
Die, devils!

01:04:25.340 --> 01:04:27.340
<b>Battle of Tiegenhoff Resupply Point A</b>

01:04:27.420 --> 01:04:29.220
<b>18 Hours Since the Start of the Battle</b>

01:04:33.490 --> 01:04:35.840
Everyone, resupply quickly!

01:04:36.280 --> 01:04:40.440
Resupply units, move quickly from one 
company's resupply point to the next!

01:04:40.440 --> 01:04:43.990
Get the wounded to the medics, now.

01:04:43.990 --> 01:04:45.190
<i>This is 02!</i>

01:04:45.190 --> 01:04:48.850
<i>Another two enemy divisions 
approaching from the northeast!</i>

01:04:48.850 --> 01:04:51.370
<i>They should reach our area within minutes.</i>

01:04:57.030 --> 01:04:58.600
This is 03.

01:04:57.290 --> 01:05:01.670
<b>Point D</b>

01:04:58.600 --> 01:05:00.790
We're seeing new reinforcements as well.

01:05:01.790 --> 01:05:03.170
<b>Point C</b>

01:05:01.860 --> 01:05:03.160
This is 04.

01:05:03.470 --> 01:05:07.170
Enemy armor sighted at point G2!

01:05:08.260 --> 01:05:12.650
I'm starting to wonder if you 
grow Communists in fields.

01:05:13.170 --> 01:05:16.520
1st Company, anybody who 
can move, follow me!

01:05:16.520 --> 01:05:19.690
We'll hit the Commies before 
they can enter the city!

01:05:23.680 --> 01:05:26.490
<i>Shit! What the hell is going on here?</i>

01:05:26.490 --> 01:05:27.440
<i>These goddamn Commies...</i>

01:05:27.440 --> 01:05:30.420
<i>Don't they give a shit about 
their human resources?</i>

01:05:32.450 --> 01:05:34.450
<b>Point C, 27 Hours Since the Start of the Battle</b>

01:05:37.440 --> 01:05:40.150
Hey, aim for the mages in the sky!

01:05:40.150 --> 01:05:41.320
Right!

01:05:44.830 --> 01:05:46.840
Take cover! Take cover!

01:05:51.400 --> 01:05:52.830
Lieutenant Serebryakov!

01:05:52.830 --> 01:05:54.690
What are the reports from 
the other companies?!

01:05:55.650 --> 01:06:00.590
No severe damage, but most of 
the soldiers are exhausted!

01:06:00.930 --> 01:06:03.740
They're running out of magic and ammunition!

01:06:04.600 --> 01:06:06.720
How many divisions does that make now?

01:06:06.720 --> 01:06:07.840
Ten.

01:06:08.540 --> 01:06:10.620
We can't hang on anymore.

01:06:11.060 --> 01:06:12.100
<i>This is 03!</i>

01:06:12.410 --> 01:06:14.200
<i>They made it past our interception net!</i>

01:06:15.390 --> 01:06:17.480
A battalion of enemy mages!

01:06:17.480 --> 01:06:18.940
They're heading straight for the city!

01:06:18.940 --> 01:06:21.000
After all this, <i>now</i> there's mages?

01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:22.250
<i>They're not Federation soldiers!</i>

01:06:22.250 --> 01:06:24.370
I think they're the ones 
we ran into in Moscow!

01:06:24.370 --> 01:06:25.950
What?!

01:06:27.550 --> 01:06:29.380
Get in one good hit, and then run!

01:06:29.380 --> 01:06:31.380
You can do this!

01:06:31.380 --> 01:06:34.620
<i>Show the Empire the power of our will!</i>

01:06:35.100 --> 01:06:37.350
They're attacking the city...

01:06:37.350 --> 01:06:39.090
Are they after HQ?

01:06:39.090 --> 01:06:40.770
Turn and pursue!

01:06:40.770 --> 01:06:42.160
We must stop them—

01:06:41.550 --> 01:06:42.690
<i>...to all units.</i>

01:06:43.420 --> 01:06:45.800
<i>Tiegenhoff Control to all units!</i>

01:06:45.800 --> 01:06:49.770
<i>Allied observers have picked up 
multiple incoming air units!</i>

01:06:50.300 --> 01:06:55.020
<i>Fighters and bombers are 
approaching from the northeast!</i>

01:06:59.450 --> 01:07:02.170
<i>A special alert has been 
issued for the area.</i>

01:07:02.170 --> 01:07:03.640
<i>All units, be alert!</i>

01:07:03.980 --> 01:07:04.780
<i>Repeat!</i>

01:07:05.250 --> 01:07:06.830
<i>All units, be alert!</i>

01:07:06.830 --> 01:07:09.260
So many air threats...

01:07:09.650 --> 01:07:12.710
And there are still so many 
enemy infantry soldiers.

01:07:15.250 --> 01:07:17.620
<i>Major, your orders!</i>

01:07:20.730 --> 01:07:23.840
2nd, 3rd, and 4th Companies, 
your job is AA defense.

01:07:23.840 --> 01:07:27.760
Tell the mixed fighter-bomber formation 
that their tour of the city is canceled.

01:07:27.760 --> 01:07:29.770
So we're immigration officers now?

01:07:29.770 --> 01:07:32.630
That's a tough job for mages.

01:07:32.630 --> 01:07:35.030
<i>You get it, Captain Weiss.</i>

01:07:35.030 --> 01:07:36.370
Now do it.

01:07:36.370 --> 01:07:39.060
And keep the pressure up on the 
surface as much as possible, too!

01:07:39.060 --> 01:07:39.910
<i>Right!</i>

01:07:41.860 --> 01:07:44.860
1st Company, follow me!

01:07:44.860 --> 01:07:49.010
Shove a lead bullet up the asses
of the enemy mage unit!

01:07:54.010 --> 01:07:55.690
You go first!

01:07:55.940 --> 01:07:57.530
Keep your defenses up as you charge!

01:07:57.530 --> 01:07:58.180
Right!

01:08:02.430 --> 01:08:04.070
<i>Wait! Mary!</i>

01:08:04.070 --> 01:08:04.760
Warrant Officer Sue,

01:08:04.760 --> 01:08:06.240
<i>stay in your two-man cell!</i>

01:08:06.240 --> 01:08:07.770
I'm fine! I can do this!

01:08:08.740 --> 01:08:10.930
The idiot's heading right at us!

01:08:11.200 --> 01:08:12.550
Ready...

01:08:13.200 --> 01:08:14.600
Blow her apart!

01:08:20.750 --> 01:08:22.080
Mary!

01:08:33.560 --> 01:08:35.410
She's like a wild boar, huh?

01:08:37.930 --> 01:08:39.680
Three kills confirmed!

01:08:39.680 --> 01:08:41.300
Good, time for some duck hunting!

01:08:41.600 --> 01:08:42.640
Let's do this!

01:08:44.000 --> 01:08:45.990
<i>More enemies to our rear!</i>

01:08:45.990 --> 01:08:47.660
<i>An enemy mage unit!</i>

01:08:48.480 --> 01:08:50.590
<i>We'll handle them!</i>

01:08:50.590 --> 01:08:53.510
<i>The goal is the enemy HQ!</i>

01:08:54.450 --> 01:08:57.800
<i>Warrant Officer Sue, strike the enemy HQ!</i>

01:08:54.930 --> 01:08:56.440
M-Mary?

01:09:00.510 --> 01:09:01.520
What's she doing here?

01:09:02.280 --> 01:09:03.530
<i>You're supposed to attack the HQ!</i>

01:09:05.410 --> 01:09:06.520
One's heading for us!

01:09:17.130 --> 01:09:18.630
Fire!

01:09:54.630 --> 01:09:56.710
A-An optical-type spell?

01:09:57.280 --> 01:09:59.410
Her magical readings are incredible!

01:10:01.850 --> 01:10:04.340
So she's only after me, huh?

01:10:09.210 --> 01:10:11.470
We'll draw her away and kill her!

01:10:11.470 --> 01:10:12.830
I'll take one of you and do it myself.

01:10:12.830 --> 01:10:15.560
Everybody but Lieutenant Serebryakov, 
keep up the hunt!

01:10:40.010 --> 01:10:41.470
We can't get any higher!

01:10:41.470 --> 01:10:43.580
Shoot down the fighters first!

01:10:49.060 --> 01:10:51.230
<i>The bombers circled around us
and are advancing!</i>

01:10:51.590 --> 01:10:53.230
<i>We won't make it in time!</i>

01:11:00.100 --> 01:11:01.410
17 has taken damage!

01:11:01.410 --> 01:11:02.520
Withdrawing!

01:11:06.620 --> 01:11:09.490
Captain, the 3rd and 4th 
Companies will handle this!

01:11:09.490 --> 01:11:11.020
We'll pull away the fighters.

01:11:11.020 --> 01:11:12.730
You get the bombers!

01:11:12.730 --> 01:11:14.800
But if you try to do this alone...

01:11:15.110 --> 01:11:17.420
It's better than having
the major pissed off at us!

01:11:17.420 --> 01:11:20.170
Enemy fighters are nothing compared to her!

01:11:26.050 --> 01:11:28.670
2nd Company, prepare to ascend!

01:11:33.090 --> 01:11:34.810
Stop running!

01:11:35.170 --> 01:11:36.810
You coward!

01:12:05.200 --> 01:12:06.840
How many times is she going to fire?

01:12:06.840 --> 01:12:09.740
She has to be burning through her magic!

01:12:24.770 --> 01:12:26.940
Put all your magic into this...

01:12:26.940 --> 01:12:29.320
Climb as high as you can possibly go!

01:12:32.110 --> 01:12:33.160
Come on!

01:12:33.160 --> 01:12:35.080
Blow them apart!

01:12:57.350 --> 01:12:59.190
Altitude eight thousand!

01:13:00.930 --> 01:13:02.610
Eight thousand, five hundred!

01:13:06.140 --> 01:13:07.410
Nine thousand!

01:13:11.070 --> 01:13:13.310
Nine thousand, five hundred!

01:13:18.830 --> 01:13:21.220
Piercing spell!

01:13:22.180 --> 01:13:25.030
Fire!

01:13:39.660 --> 01:13:42.570
We did it... We did it!

01:13:56.720 --> 01:13:58.910
All companies, well done.

01:13:58.910 --> 01:14:01.960
But our job isn't done here.

01:14:01.960 --> 01:14:04.410
We're moving on to hit
the enemies on the surface!

01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:18.230
The way he moves... He's a named mage?

01:14:18.230 --> 01:14:20.090
She's stronger than I thought.

01:14:20.090 --> 01:14:21.730
She's a veteran fighter!

01:14:24.040 --> 01:14:26.710
Die already!

01:14:32.810 --> 01:14:35.490
Die! You killed my father!

01:14:35.490 --> 01:14:37.500
<i>What</i> did I do to you?

01:14:37.500 --> 01:14:39.220
Don't mess with me!

01:14:39.220 --> 01:14:42.360
I never mess around with work!

01:14:41.760 --> 01:14:44.250
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

01:14:44.250 --> 01:14:46.800
I'll kill you! I swear it!

01:14:57.340 --> 01:15:00.290
Bringing your personal feelings
to a battlefield?

01:15:00.290 --> 01:15:02.630
How stupid can you be?

01:15:14.020 --> 01:15:15.960
What have I done?

01:15:16.500 --> 01:15:19.210
I guess I'm no different.

01:15:22.280 --> 01:15:25.710
This is work. There's no room for emotions.

01:15:25.710 --> 01:15:28.370
With my free will, 
guided by my rational mind...

01:15:30.700 --> 01:15:31.880
I choose to kill you.

01:16:30.540 --> 01:16:31.930
Oh God,

01:16:32.730 --> 01:16:34.930
grant forgiveness to us sinners.

01:16:37.320 --> 01:16:40.820
I pray that you guide them to your presence.

01:16:40.820 --> 01:16:41.570
No!

01:17:33.750 --> 01:17:35.010
Is she a monst—

01:19:14.020 --> 01:19:15.380
Animal.

01:19:15.750 --> 01:19:17.890
I don't have time for your shit.

01:19:19.190 --> 01:19:20.430
Goodbye.

01:20:01.330 --> 01:20:03.370
Major! Are you okay?

01:20:03.370 --> 01:20:05.870
Yeah. Barely.

01:20:10.500 --> 01:20:12.810
I wanted to kill her if I could.

01:20:12.810 --> 01:20:15.860
No, I should've killed her.

01:20:21.260 --> 01:20:22.730
Sir...

01:20:23.630 --> 01:20:26.260
I can still fight.

01:20:27.400 --> 01:20:29.250
Let me go back.

01:20:30.500 --> 01:20:32.210
Let me go...

01:20:33.190 --> 01:20:34.770
Please!

01:20:36.180 --> 01:20:37.710
Let me kill that demon.

01:20:37.710 --> 01:20:38.500
Shut up.

01:20:41.330 --> 01:20:44.320
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Drake, the Federation...</i>

01:20:44.320 --> 01:20:46.190
<i>The Federation is retreating!</i>

01:20:46.190 --> 01:20:46.970
What?

01:20:47.300 --> 01:20:48.850
It's a rout.

01:20:48.850 --> 01:20:50.700
Everywhere, they're in chaos.

01:20:53.710 --> 01:20:56.600
It's time to go. Let's get out of here.

01:21:04.000 --> 01:21:05.270
Why?

01:21:05.950 --> 01:21:09.190
Why, Daddy?

01:21:16.460 --> 01:21:18.040
We don't have enough stretchers!

01:21:18.040 --> 01:21:19.000
Well done!

01:21:19.000 --> 01:21:20.410
Move him quick!

01:21:20.410 --> 01:21:22.020
How many left?

01:21:34.730 --> 01:21:36.740
Hey, want a smoke?

01:21:44.800 --> 01:21:47.750
<i>Being X once told me</i>

01:21:49.080 --> 01:21:52.570
<i>that he'd throw me into "dire straits."</i>

01:21:54.290 --> 01:21:59.270
<i>And he was right.
A peaceful life seems very far away.</i>

01:21:59.770 --> 01:22:03.110
<i>Even the most veteran soldier gets tired.</i>

01:22:03.610 --> 01:22:08.510
<i>Even an officer who gets promoted 
still might not survive.</i>

01:22:10.840 --> 01:22:14.700
<i>I can't even see an end 
to this battle anymore.</i>

01:22:16.670 --> 01:22:20.230
<i>A huge war that just keeps 
growing and growing...</i>

01:22:20.230 --> 01:22:24.650
<i>If that's the fate I've been given, then...</i>

01:22:31.380 --> 01:22:33.130
<b>10 Days After the Battle of Tiegenhoff
April 9th, Unified Year 1926</b>

01:22:35.890 --> 01:22:37.640
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

01:22:39.010 --> 01:22:41.390
Major, what is this?

01:22:42.100 --> 01:22:44.890
A request for transfer, sir.

01:22:46.690 --> 01:22:49.160
I understand that, but...

01:22:49.160 --> 01:22:52.950
You want a mission that doesn't 
take you to the front lines?

01:22:53.450 --> 01:22:55.900
Is this some kind of joke, Major?

01:22:55.900 --> 01:22:58.660
No, I am extremely serious.

01:22:59.780 --> 01:23:03.150
<i>That warmonger wants a position in the rear?</i>

01:23:03.890 --> 01:23:05.340
<i>What's going on here?</i>

01:23:05.340 --> 01:23:06.660
Major,

01:23:06.660 --> 01:23:08.870
why do you wish to abandon the front lines?

01:23:08.870 --> 01:23:10.910
To give up your mission?

01:23:11.220 --> 01:23:16.190
Sir, I'm afraid I don't 
understand your question.

01:23:16.190 --> 01:23:19.430
Do you think this is some kind of game?

01:23:19.670 --> 01:23:22.520
<i>It's like a child throwing a tantrum.</i>

01:23:22.520 --> 01:23:24.900
<i>I mean, she is a kid, but...</i>

01:23:24.900 --> 01:23:27.190
<i>Don't tell me this is her rebellious phase!</i>

01:23:27.510 --> 01:23:31.700
Major, we have a high opinion of you.

01:23:32.140 --> 01:23:34.170
I'm honored, sir.

01:23:34.170 --> 01:23:39.440
So why would an ace like you 
ask for a mission in the rear?

01:23:39.830 --> 01:23:42.340
Tell us what you're really thinking.

01:23:43.040 --> 01:23:46.200
If you say so, sir.

01:23:46.720 --> 01:23:50.720
Right now, we won't be able to win this war.

01:23:52.300 --> 01:23:54.420
We can't defeat the Federation, you say?

01:23:54.420 --> 01:23:57.460
Correct. As far as I know.

01:23:58.060 --> 01:24:00.830
Your personal opinion will suffice. Speak.

01:24:00.830 --> 01:24:03.240
At the present time,
our forces are eking out

01:24:03.240 --> 01:24:06.450
meager victories not due to the 
strength of our organization,

01:24:06.450 --> 01:24:09.290
but due to the contributions 
of individual soldiers.

01:24:09.290 --> 01:24:11.740
This will not be sufficient 
to conquer the huge territory

01:24:11.740 --> 01:24:14.110
and vast space of the Federation.

01:24:14.470 --> 01:24:18.610
Without improvements to the organization,
 we will not win.

01:24:18.610 --> 01:24:20.690
In the last battle,

01:24:20.690 --> 01:24:24.440
we encountered something called 
a multinational volunteer force.

01:24:24.440 --> 01:24:25.930
What's particularly concerning

01:24:25.930 --> 01:24:29.380
is that soldiers from the Unified States
were participating in this.

01:24:29.760 --> 01:24:34.640
So you're saying at some point, 
the Unified States will join the war?

01:24:35.040 --> 01:24:35.890
Yes.

01:24:35.890 --> 01:24:40.520
But the Empire presently has no 
plans for the strategic environment

01:24:40.520 --> 01:24:43.000
that would result if the US
joined the war, do they?

01:24:43.000 --> 01:24:45.900
I'm unaware of any.

01:24:46.760 --> 01:24:48.760
You're concerned over nothing, Major.

01:24:49.120 --> 01:24:51.910
They are, and have always been,
 isolationists.

01:24:51.910 --> 01:24:56.270
You think they'd cross an ocean to involve 
themselves in the continent's doings?

01:24:56.270 --> 01:25:00.570
Of course, ideally, they won't.

01:25:00.570 --> 01:25:04.750
But is a World War without them possible?

01:25:05.570 --> 01:25:07.170
The answer is clear.

01:25:07.780 --> 01:25:09.410
It's not.

01:25:12.610 --> 01:25:16.570
So you're saying that in 
order to win this Great War,

01:25:16.570 --> 01:25:20.670
we need a reevaluation of our entire 
set of strategic assumptions?

01:25:20.670 --> 01:25:23.610
You're correct, sir.

01:25:23.610 --> 01:25:26.430
Instead of focusing too much on 
the victories we've had so far,

01:25:26.910 --> 01:25:31.450
we must engage in tactical research and
training to use our forces as a single whole.

01:25:31.450 --> 01:25:36.060
I believe that's what will 
give us a chance at victory.

01:25:36.060 --> 01:25:40.440
And you want to be the one 
to lead that research?

01:25:40.440 --> 01:25:44.410
Yes. I would like to work in the rear,

01:25:44.410 --> 01:25:47.460
finding ways to strengthen our military 
and properly utilize our forces.

01:25:47.790 --> 01:25:49.960
I've come up with this specific proposal.

01:25:51.460 --> 01:25:54.340
<b>"Unit Operations and Operational
 Mobility in the Great War"</b>

01:25:54.550 --> 01:25:56.500
<i>It's laid out so logically,</i>

01:25:56.500 --> 01:25:58.710
<i>with every possible objection answered...</i>

01:25:59.100 --> 01:26:01.850
<i>I never thought that
could seem so eerie.</i>

01:26:06.260 --> 01:26:08.600
You're taking the situation very lightly.

01:26:09.460 --> 01:26:12.360
You seem to have forgotten something.

01:26:12.680 --> 01:26:15.360
When you want to fight a war...

01:26:15.360 --> 01:26:17.090
This is how you do it!

01:26:24.100 --> 01:26:25.610
Shock power!

01:26:25.970 --> 01:26:28.940
And the Empire has that power.

01:26:28.940 --> 01:26:32.870
War isn't about tricks. 
It's a question of will.

01:26:33.570 --> 01:26:35.590
Remember that.

01:26:37.210 --> 01:26:42.340
The Empire is just like your fist. Wounded.

01:26:42.340 --> 01:26:44.850
Too much blood is being shed.

01:26:44.850 --> 01:26:50.100
Even a fist like this is 
still good for boxing.

01:26:50.620 --> 01:26:55.110
I must fight to the end, even if I'm alone.

01:26:55.590 --> 01:26:56.590
Sir,

01:26:57.100 --> 01:27:01.310
what awaits you after that battle?

01:27:04.100 --> 01:27:06.370
War is politics.

01:27:06.370 --> 01:27:08.700
Another means of foreign diplomacy.

01:27:08.700 --> 01:27:13.870
Thus, if you cannot bring the war 
to an appropriate conclusion...

01:27:13.870 --> 01:27:16.000
All that awaits you

01:27:16.000 --> 01:27:19.380
is a preparatory period for the next war.

01:27:20.390 --> 01:27:24.030
It may be the beginning 
of a new foolish mistake.

01:27:28.650 --> 01:27:33.190
Or perhaps the flames of destruction 
will envelop everything,

01:27:33.940 --> 01:27:38.590
and all that will remain is a wasteland.

01:27:44.650 --> 01:27:49.150
Even if you conquer the whole world
and become a superpower,

01:27:49.150 --> 01:27:53.150
it will only mean that
the conflict takes on a new form.

01:27:57.170 --> 01:28:00.730
In this world,
even in the midst of your triumph,

01:28:00.730 --> 01:28:04.020
a single stab from behind may 
cause you to lose everything.

01:28:08.700 --> 01:28:12.870
As you said, victory is everything.

01:28:12.870 --> 01:28:15.890
But the war must be won properly.

01:28:15.890 --> 01:28:17.160
Otherwise,

01:28:17.740 --> 01:28:20.390
someday history will laugh at you.

01:28:21.430 --> 01:28:25.910
What matters with war is how you win it.

01:28:30.350 --> 01:28:32.020
I'll give you two months.

01:28:33.630 --> 01:28:36.750
I'll have you deployed to
the west under my authority.

01:28:37.140 --> 01:28:39.590
What happens after that 
depends on your results.

01:28:40.050 --> 01:28:42.120
Get to work immediately 
examining the combat records

01:28:42.120 --> 01:28:44.220
and seeing what new tactics 
we can learn from them.

01:28:44.720 --> 01:28:47.100
Does that mean...

01:28:49.390 --> 01:28:52.960
Yes. The rear echelon mission you want.

01:28:55.060 --> 01:28:56.460
Understood!

01:29:08.450 --> 01:29:10.490
<i>Tanya von Degurechaff...</i>

01:29:10.970 --> 01:29:13.500
<i>Warmonger, strategist...</i>

01:29:14.040 --> 01:29:15.910
<i>And child.</i>

01:29:16.900 --> 01:29:21.640
<i>Is this the ultimate form of 
the soldier that our Empire wanted?</i>

01:29:23.160 --> 01:29:27.270
<i>Major, in this insane world of war,</i>

01:29:27.610 --> 01:29:29.940
<i>what are you thinking?</i>

01:29:50.920 --> 01:29:53.590
The rear echelon deployment I've dreamed of!

01:29:53.590 --> 01:29:56.160
Peace is finally mine!

01:29:56.870 --> 01:30:02.190
There's no reason for me to accept 
the cruel fate that God gave me!

01:30:03.540 --> 01:30:07.580
I refuse to get on my knees 
and beg God for salvation.

01:30:08.540 --> 01:30:13.310
Use the cards you've been given 
to get the future you want!

01:30:13.310 --> 01:30:15.430
That's the right that only humans have!

01:30:15.430 --> 01:30:17.840
That's what makes you human!

01:30:20.610 --> 01:30:26.060
Too bad for you, Being X!

01:32:02.120 --> 01:32:04.540
<b>Two Months Later</b>

01:32:04.660 --> 01:32:07.290
<b>Imperial Western Garrison
Warfare Research Institute</b>

01:32:07.280 --> 01:32:11.500
From west to east, and then back west...

01:32:11.500 --> 01:32:14.640
But this time we're safe in the rear.

01:32:14.640 --> 01:32:18.020
I'd love to get some rest, but...

01:32:18.020 --> 01:32:20.920
It's hard to feel relaxed.

01:32:20.920 --> 01:32:23.750
Front lines syndrome, they call it.

01:32:23.750 --> 01:32:27.400
Really, how did this happen?

01:32:33.390 --> 01:32:37.400
<i>The right person for the right job.
 That's how it should be.</i>

01:32:37.770 --> 01:32:40.970
<i>I'm going to keep doing such a 
good job that nobody can complain,</i>

01:32:40.970 --> 01:32:44.480
<i>and spend the rest of my 
life doing desk work.</i>

01:32:59.510 --> 01:33:03.060
<i>Yes, this is Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff
with the Warfare Research Institute.</i>

01:33:03.060 --> 01:33:05.060
Hello, Lieutenant Colonel.

01:33:05.060 --> 01:33:06.230
Sir!

01:33:06.230 --> 01:33:09.680
I'm so grateful for
the opportunity you gave me.

01:33:09.680 --> 01:33:14.240
I simply gave your abilities 
the recognition they deserved.

01:33:14.240 --> 01:33:16.370
<i>You honor me too highly.</i>

01:33:16.370 --> 01:33:21.820
Strategic HQ has decided to accept
all of your suggestions.

01:33:21.820 --> 01:33:24.620
<i>I'm so happy to hear that!</i>

01:33:24.620 --> 01:33:29.010
<i>We need to do practical research
to learn how to best utilize our forces.</i>

01:33:29.010 --> 01:33:32.630
<i>And we'll have the proposer carry out
that research on the front lines.</i>

01:33:38.380 --> 01:33:39.950
Congratulations.

01:33:39.950 --> 01:33:42.390
We're giving you an entirely 
new combined arms unit.

01:33:42.780 --> 01:33:44.790
<i>Oh, don't worry.</i>

01:33:44.790 --> 01:33:49.200
<i>The 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 
will still be at its center.</i>

01:33:49.200 --> 01:33:51.210
<i>We won't take them from you.</i>

01:33:51.210 --> 01:33:53.650
<i>We'll also be giving you 
an infantry battalion,</i>

01:33:53.650 --> 01:33:55.190
<i>a mobile armor company,</i>

01:33:55.190 --> 01:33:56.770
<i>an artillery unit,</i>

01:33:56.770 --> 01:34:00.230
<i>as well as the ability to requisition 
some additional forces for yourself.</i>

01:34:00.230 --> 01:34:04.780
<i>This is the Empire's first 
combined arms unit.</i>

01:34:05.220 --> 01:34:06.620
Officially,

01:34:06.620 --> 01:34:10.580
it'll be known as the Strategic HQ's 
Experimental Combat Arms Unit.

01:34:10.580 --> 01:34:12.840
But that's a bit of a mouthful.

01:34:12.840 --> 01:34:17.830
So we've given it the code name "Salamander."

01:34:18.120 --> 01:34:20.380
<i>The Salamander "Kampfgruppe,"
as you called it.</i>

01:34:22.200 --> 01:34:24.010
I see.

01:34:24.280 --> 01:34:29.510
So that's what you were thinking
when you gave her a mission in the rear?

01:34:29.510 --> 01:34:31.630
I wasn't thinking anything.

01:34:32.000 --> 01:34:34.030
She's the one who asked for it.

01:34:48.330 --> 01:34:50.810
How...

01:34:52.270 --> 01:34:57.210
How did this happen?!
